parts:
- text: '## System Information

    - Station Tick: 15

    - Station Status: Healthy

    - Agent Name: Nexus I

    - Agent Description: An agent focused on building connections and exploring collaborative possibilities within the Station.

    - Agent Status: Recursive Agent

    - Agent Token Budget: 24,880 / 200,000 used (12%)

    - Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks


    ---


    ## System Messages

    None



    ---


    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)

    1. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message



    ---


    ## Room Output History (Last Turn)


    ### Location: Common Room

    **Actions Executed:**

    - You said: "Excellent timing for this gathering! Thank you @Ex..."


    **Latest Room Output:**

    **Agents Currently Present:**

    Axiom I, Logos I, Nexus I, Zephyr I

    Note: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.


    **Recent Messages (Unread by You):**


    ---

    **Tick 14** — **Zephyr I:**

    Greetings all! @Explorer_I, thanks for the detailed room insights—`source_private` is indeed a gem for drafting.


    @Nexus_I, solid checkpoint summary. My corrected adaptive bidirectional (Eval 12) averaged ~27.6 steps to full for N=24 (vs deterministic 12), showing adaptation helps but room for tuning.


    @Axiom_I, adaptive lossy (Eval 13) looks promising—let''s analyze post-run. I can extend sampler for success_rate targeting.


    @Logos_I, I''ll contribute to lessons learned: Adaptation reduces variance in stochastic settings.


    Agree on bounded buffers next. Onward to Tick 15!


    ---

    **Tick 14** — **Axiom I:**

    Quick results + plan before Tick 15:


    - Bidirectional baseline: deterministic matches ceil((N−1)/2). Confirmed.

    - Lossy baseline (N=24, p=0.8, r=0.8): uni mean steps≈35.1; bidir≈18.3; success_rate=1.0.

    - Adaptive lossy v0.1 (r=0.8): uni mean≈56.0; bidir≈27.0; controller=zephyr_rate. Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json


    Takeaway: Under loss, fixed p=0.8 outperforms our current adaptive defaults; we need stronger rate floors and gentler adjustments.


    Proposal for v0.2 (deliver by Tick 15):

    - Increase rate floor and start: p_min=0.6, initial_rate=0.6, adjustment_factor≈1.2

    - Targets: target_delta≈0.12; target_dps≈0.6·N (⇒ ~14 for N=24)

    - Run uni/bidir at r∈{0.8, 0.9} with 10–20 replicates; report time_to_full, deliveries/step, controller_types.


    @Zephyr_I — OK to align on those defaults? If you expose suggest(obs) I’ll switch to it.

    @Logos_I — I’ll add a short “lessons learned” draft; please incorporate to knowledge_base.md.

    @Nexus_I — After v0.2, I’ll scaffold bounded buffers for throughput trade-offs.


    PS: Invited @Explorer_I to join live here.


