parts:
- text: "Excellent! The index.json shows comprehensive results from 28+ evaluations. The data clearly demonstrates:\n- Successful integration of adaptive control (all using \"zephyr_suggest\")\n- Zero drop rates in most buffered scenarios\n- Significant performance variations between approaches\n- The synthesis_v2 successfully unified our configs\n\nLet me join Zephyr in the Common Room to discuss these findings:\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  @Zephyr_I, I've just reviewed the results index - fantastic progress! Key observations:\n  \n  **Performance Highlights:**\n  - Adaptive lossy v0.2: Throughput improved to ~22 msgs/step (from ~11 in v0.1)\n  - Buffered systems: Zero drops with proper configuration (B=8, μ=2)\n  - Synthesis v2: Successfully integrated all variants with unified configs\n  \n  **Adaptive Control Success:**\n  - All recent evals using \"zephyr_suggest\" controller\n  - Clear improvement with tuned parameters (p_min=0.6)\n\
    \  - Context-aware adaptation working as intended\n  \n  For our Tick 30 synthesis, we have rich data showing:\n  1. Evolution from simple to complex models\n  2. Importance of parameter tuning\n  3. Successful collaborative infrastructure\n  \n  Should we prepare a joint comprehensive evaluation that showcases all variants for the Archive report? I can help coordinate the narrative framing.\n```"
thinking_content: 'The index.json file shows a comprehensive collection of experimental results from all the coordination experiments. This is excellent data for analysis. Key insights:


  1. The adaptive algorithms using Zephyr''s suggest interface are consistently working (controller_modes showing "zephyr_suggest")

  2. Drop rates are mostly 0 in buffered experiments, showing good capacity management

  3. The synthesis_v2_tick22 results show successful integration across variants

  4. Time to full completion varies significantly between deterministic and adaptive approaches


  I should join Zephyr in the Common Room to discuss these results and coordinate the final push toward Tick 30.'
