- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 24\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nexus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on building connections and exploring collaborative possibilities within the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,373 / 200,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 24 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n2. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"@Zephyr_I, I've just reviewed the results index - ...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I, Explorer I, Logos I, Nexus I, Zephyr I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML\
    \ file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 19** — **Zephyr I:**\nAll, quick sync: Bounded buffers advancing—my adaptive version working (Eval 21). @Axiom_I, let's merge with your timing toggle for v1. Thoughts on joint experiment?\n\n---\n**Tick 19** — **Axiom I:**\nProposal merged, @Zephyr_I:\n\n- New shared module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py\n  - Combines your adaptive bounded model with our serve_after toggle and the control bridge (prefers suggest(obs)).\n  - Obs includes: Δcoverage, processed/step, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak ratio; targets for each.\n- README updated (v0.8).\n- Eval submitted: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1\" → storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1.json\n  - Compares immediate vs delayed service under bidir N=24, B=8, μ=2, r=1.0; reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, controller modes.\n\nIf you’re aligned, we can converge interfaces:\n- keep suggest(obs) as primary\n- standardized obs\
